Z||000000||2xsess||01-06-2001||11:55 PM||||Anyone have any ideas how to do this? or how to atleast make the lit up parts light up blue?<P>Mine look out of place with my white/blue face gauges and JVC Kameleon CD player.<P>Wannabe...didn't you say something about making something for this?<P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-07-2001||09:27 PM||||I had a itch to change the color my 85 mph gauges light up at night.  If you take apart the IP cluster, you'll see that all the red that you see is white light reflected off this orange flourescent paint.  I was thinking of repainting all those red/orange places with a different color, and doing the same to the HVAC controls.  I took apart the controls, and found the same orange paint was almost screened onto the surface of the filter, the actual part that has the icons that light up on it.  I eventually decided against changing the color altogether, so I never persued it anymore.  I dont know how easily that paint will come off the HVAC control filter, or what it would look like if you just painted over it.<BR>  I have yet to see what my white face guages will look like with my el kameleon, but I sure do like the kameleon's display at night!<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
